# Everything in this repo runs on Linux, so everything checks out with LF
# regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf. This is not cosmetic: a CRLF line
# ending in install.sh makes the kernel read the shebang as `/bin/bash\r` and
# `sudo ./install.sh` fails with "No such file or directory", which is an
# invisible fault in every editor. tests/test_packaging.py checks the working
# tree for the same thing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text. Never touch the bytes.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
